-- title:
--   Inertia fixes square roots of p-adic units, p odd
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime with $p \neq 2$, let $d \in \mathbb{Q}_p$ satisfy $\|d\|_{+} = 1$ (the non-negative-real-valued norm of $d$ equals $1$, i.e. $d$ is a $p$-adic unit), and let $s$ be an element of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_p =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ_[p]` with $s^2$ equal to the image of $d$ under the structure map $\mathbb{Q}_p \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}_p$. The assertion is that every $\mathbb{Q}_p$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_p$ lying in the subgroup `inertiaSubgroupIn` of the valuation subring [`padicIntegers p`](def/GaloisRep_CompletionBridge.html#L20) — that is, the image, under the inclusion of the decomposition subgroup of [`padicIntegers p`](def/GaloisRep_CompletionBridge.html#L20) over $\mathbb{Q}_p$ into the full automorphism group, of the inertia subgroup of that valuation subring over $\mathbb{Q}_p$, where [`padicIntegers p`](def/GaloisRep_CompletionBridge.html#L20) is the valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_p$ attached to its canonical $\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}$-valued valuation — satisfies $\tau(s) = s$. Equivalently, $\mathbb{Q}_p(\sqrt{d})$ is unramified over $\mathbb{Q}_p$ for $d$ a unit and $p$ odd, stated in the form that inertia acts trivially on a chosen square root.
--
--   This is the standard fact that, for odd residue characteristic, the quadratic extension generated by a square root of a unit is unramified, expressed as triviality of the inertia action on the square root. It is used in the local analysis of curves with multiplicative reduction, where the isomorphism with the Tate curve is defined over $\mathbb{Q}_p(\sqrt{d})$ for a unit $d$; it is cited by the two statements producing a Galois-equivariant identification of the $\ell$-torsion in that situation ([`WeierstrassCurve.exists_addEquiv_torsionBy_localGaloisToGlobal_smul_eq_of_dvd_discr_of_eq_three`](thm.html#WeierstrassCurve.exists_addEquiv_torsionBy_localGaloisToGlobal_smul_eq_of_dvd_discr_of_eq_three) and [`WeierstrassCurve.exists_addEquiv_torsionBy_localGaloisToGlobal_smul_eq_of_dvd_discr_of_five_le`](thm.html#WeierstrassCurve.exists_addEquiv_torsionBy_localGaloisToGlobal_smul_eq_of_dvd_discr_of_five_le)).
